r of C1: a small bedroom with a bed, a chest and a lamp.","box":[27,2,10,34,5,14],"ways_in":"Doorway (26,2..3,12) from the atrium; window (35,3..4,12)."},{"name":"Cubiculum C4 (SE)","purpose":"Mirror of C2: a bedroom with a bed, a chest and a lamp.","box":[27,2,16,34,5,21],"ways_in":"Doorway (26,2..3,18) from the atrium; window (35,3..4,18)."},{"name":"Tablinum","purpose":"The master's study on the main axis, open at both ends (to the atrium and to the garden). It holds a desk of lectern and bookshelves, scroll shelves, a chair and a brazier or lamp. Mosaic panel: white field, red and black borders, blue emblem at x17..18,z26..27. Keep the axis x15..20 clear to walk through.","box":[11,2,23,24,5,30],"ways_in":"Atrium opening (15..20,2..5,22); peristyle opening (15..20,2..5,31); doorways (10,2..3,27) to the kitchen and (25,2..3,27) to the triclinium."},{"name":"Culina (kitchen)","purpose":"Working kitchen, warm and smoky. Hearth at the west wall: pad (1..3,y2,25..27), lit campfire at (2,3,26), stone-brick-stair hood at y5 around (2,5,26) under the open flue. Counter with smoker, furnace and crafting table; water cauldron, barrels, a table.","box":[1,2,23,9,5,30],"ways_in":"Doorway (10,2..3,27) from the tablinum; opening (7..8,2..4,31) to the colonnade; window (0,3..4,26)."},{"name":"Triclinium","purpose":"Festive dining room. Three couches (red beds with dark-oak rails) on the west, north and east sides and a low table in the middle, open to the south doorway. Niche lamps; meander mosaic with an orange emblem at x29..31,z25..27.","box":[26,2,23,34,5,30],"ways_in":"Doorway (25,2..3,27) from the tablinum; opening (27..28,2..4,31) to the colonnade; window (35,3..4,26)."},{"name":"Cubiculum C5 (SW of court)","purpose":"Small bedroom off the peristyle: bed, chest, lamp.","box":[1,2,32,5,5,37],"ways_in":"Doorway (6,2..3,35) from the colonnade; window (0,3..4,35)."},{"name":"Lararium (C6)","purpose":"Quiet household shrine: an altar niche on the west wall (quartz and stone-brick stairs), candles, a bronze lantern, potted plants, an item frame.","box":[1,2,39,5,5,44],"ways_in":"Doorway (6,2..3,41) from the colonnade; window (3,3..4,45)."},{"name":"Cubiculum C7 (SE of court)","purpose":"Mirror of C5: a small bedroom with bed, chest and lamp.","box":[30,2,32,34,5,37],"ways_in":"Doorway (29,2..3,35) from the colonnade; window (35,3..4,35)."},{"name":"Storeroom C8 (apotheca)","purpose":"Store: amphorae (decorated pots), barrels, chests, sacks; plain stone-brick floor.","box":[30,2,39,34,5,44],"ways_in":"Doorway (29,2..3,41) from the colonnade; window (32,3..4,45)."},{"name":"Peristyle colonnade (covered walkway)","purpose":"Calm, shaded cloister around the open garden. Benches, potted plants and hanging bronze lamps between the white columns, statues at the corners (8,33) and (27,33). The garden court x11..24,z35..41 in the middle is open sky and belongs to the peristyle part; keep it unbuilt.","box":[7,2,32,28,5,44],"ways_in":"Tablinum opening (15..20,2..5,31); kitchen opening (7..8,2..4,31); triclinium opening (27..28,2..4,31); doorways (6,2..3,35), (6,2..3,41), (29,2..3,35), (29,2..3,41); rear door (17..18,2..3,45)."}],"entrance":[17,1,0],"concept_subject":"A Roman town house (domus) seen from its street, 36 blocks wide and 48 deep, single storey, symmetrical about its centre line. The street front is a long cream plaster wall on a stone-brick plinth, with a red-painted dado (the lower two courses) and a cut-sandstone cornice. Under a low red-tile gable roof (brick-red and granite tiles, a mud-brick eave, a pale ridge), the wall is pierced by four open shop windows with masonry counters, clay jars and spruce shutters folded flat on both sides, two on each side of the middle. In the centre a four-wide recessed entrance passage (the fauces) is flanked by two white marble pilasters, with a three-step white pediment above. Two double spruce doors stand set back inside, with a fanlight over them, reached by a stone step from the sidewalk, and bronze lampstands and potted ferns stand beside it. Behind the front block the roof falls inward to the atrium, a bright hall with a black-and-white checker mosaic, open to the sky through an 8x6 square opening. Four dark-oak Tuscan columns stand at its corners, and under it is a shallow rain pool (the impluvium) with a white marble coping; the four small red-tile roof strips slope toward the opening. Straight on the axis, the tablinum (study) opens through white pilasters to a peristyle: a covered colonnade of 18 white marble columns with chiselled capitals, a continuous white architrave and red-tile sheds sloping inward. In the open garden court are two symmetrical parterre beds with clipped hedges of azalea and red and blue flowers, a white marble fountain basin with a central pedestal and water bowls, white statues on stone plinths, rose bushes and potted plants, and bronze lanterns hanging between the columns. Small barred windows, a triclinium with three red couches, cubicula, a kitchen with a hearth and a tall brick chimney stack on the west side, and a rear service door close the block.","concept_size":"36 wide (x), 48 deep (z), single storey (walls to y6, ridges to y9)","concept_palette":"Walls: smooth_sandstone / end_stone_bricks / sandstone (cream plaster); dado: red_terracotta; plinth: stone_bricks; cornice: cut_sandstone; columns, pilasters, architrave, fountain and statues: quartz_block / quartz_pillar / chiseled_quartz_block / smooth_quartz / diorite_wall; roofs: red-tile palette (bricks, granite, polished_granite, mangrove_planks, mud_bricks eave); ceilings, doors and furniture: spruce_planks, spruce_door, dark_oak_log/planks; bronze: copper_lantern, copper_chain, copper_bars, cut_copper_slab; floors: quartz_block / polished_blackstone / red_terracotta / black_terracotta / white_terracotta / yellow_terracotta / blue_glazed_terracotta / orange_glazed_terracotta; garden: grass_block, gravel, azalea_leaves, flowering_azalea_leaves, poppy, azure_bluet, allium, cornflower, rose_bush, lilac; water: water, water_cauldron.","parts":[{"name":"Villa shell (podium, walls, floors, ceilings, all openings)","module":"parts/shell.mjs","scope":"Foundation y0 across x0..35, z2..45, and the mosaic floors at y1 per the ROOMS table. Every wall line y1..6 (outer walls z=2, z=45, x=0, x=35; inner walls z=9, 15, 22, 31, x=8, 9, 10, 15, 20, 25, 26, 27, 6, 29) using wallCell roles (stone_bricks plinth, red_terracotta dado y2..3, plaster hash y4..5, cut_sandstone cornice y6). Leave every opening in the OPENINGS table unset, including the plane z=4 in the fauces. Fauces pilasters at (15,z2) and (20,z2). A spruce_planks ceiling at y6 over all rooms and walkways, with the holes at compluvium x14..21,z13..18, garden x11..24,z35..41 and flue (2,6,26). Leave unset: the garden floor and the pool cells x15..20,z14..17 at y1 (P4 and P5 fill them). Use wallLine, wallCell, pilaster, mosaic."},{"name":"Tile roofs sloping inward","module":"parts/roofs.mjs","scope":"All 16 roof pieces R1..R16 from the plan table, at y7..9 (first roof course on the y6 cornice). Use `mcd roof` or roof() with the temple preset as a base (red-tile palette) and the per-piece style, ridge and low-side overrides: gables on R1..R3 and R8..R10, R15, R16; sheds on R4..R7 (atrium pinwheel) and R11..R14 (peristyle pinwheel), low edge toward the court. Dry-run first, no bypass flags except the documented `--why` for overhang 0; overhang only on R1 north (1). Keep the compluvium hole x14..21,z13..18 and the garden hole x11..24,z35..41 open. Then the fauces pediment (x14..21, y7..9, z=2..3, quartz stairs and smooth_quartz) and the kitchen chimney stack (hollow 3x3 stone_bricks x1..3,z25..27,y6..9, core (2,6..9,26) air)."},{"name":"Street front and fauces","module":"parts/street.mjs","scope":"Sidewalk z0..1 y0 (andesite 60 / polished_andesite 40) with the kerb row at z=0 (stone_brick_slab bottom, y1, except x16..19). Entrance step: stone_brick_stairs facing south at (16..19,1,1). In the fauces plane z=4: two doorPairs of open spruce doors (x16..19, y2..3), spruce_trapdoor fanlights at y4, a dark_oak_planks lintel at y5. Four shopWindow counters (stone_brick_slab bottom at y2 across x3..5, 10..13, 22..25, 30..32) with a decorated_pot each, and the shutters: open spruce_trapdoors facing north in z=1, y3..4, at x2,6, 9,14, 21,26, 29,33. Lampstands at (14,1) and (21,1), potted ferns at (13,1) and (22,1)."},{"name":"Atrium and interior joinery","module":"parts/atrium.mjs","scope":"Impluvium: water at y1 on x15..20,z14..17, smooth_quartz_slab coping at y2 on the ring x14..21,z13..18 except the corners. Four tuscanColumns at (14,13),(21,13),(14,18),(21,18); dark_oak_log edge beams at y6 around the compluvium. Statue niches at (11,12) and (24,12). Quartz pilasters at x15 and x20 on z=9 and at x14 and x21 on z=22. Every interior doorway marked P4 in OPENINGS: (15,2..3,6), (20,2..3,6), (8,2..3,6), (27,2..3,6), (9,2..3,12), (9,2..3,18), (26,2..3,12), (26,2..3,18), (10,2..3,27), (25,2..3,27). Atrium hangLamps at (12,11),(23,11),(12,20),(23,20), potted plants at the four atrium corners."},{"name":"Peristyle colonnade and garden","module":"parts/peristyle.mjs","scope":"18 white columns on the rectangle x10..25, z34..42 (x in {10,13,16,19,22,25} on z=34 and z=42; z in {34,36,38,40,42} on x=10 and x=25), architrave smooth_quartz at y6 along the rectangle, a smooth_stone stylobate at y1 under it. Quartz pilasters at x14 and x21 on z=31. Doorways on x=6 and x=29 at z=35 and z=41. Garden court x11..24,z35..41: grass lawn, gravel ring, two gardenBeds (x12..14 and x21..23, z36..40) with azalea hedges and flowers, fountain basin x15..20,z36..40 with water and pedestal (17..18,38), statues at (13,38),(22,38),(8,33),(27,33), rose_bush at (11,35),(24,35), lilac at (11,41),(24,41). Quartz-stair benches at (13,33),(22,33),(13,43),(22,43). Twelve colonnade hangLamps at (12,33),(15,33),(20,33),(23,33),(8,36),(8,40),(27,36),(27,40),(12,43),(15,43),(20,43),(23,43)."},{"name":"Finish: grilles, rear door, lamps, plants, final look","module":"parts/finish.mjs","scope":"copper_bars windowGrilles in every x=0 and x=35 window (z=12, 18, 26, 35) and the back-wall windows (3,3..4,45) and (32,3..4,45). Rear doorPair at (17..18,2..3,45) and the rear lane z46..47 (gravel 70 / dirt_path 30), lampstands at (16,44),(19,44), pots at (16,46),(19,46). Remaining potted plants: (14,32),(21,32),(9,33),(26,33),(9,43),(26,43). Then render from the street, down the axis, and from above, and fix what fell between the parts."}]}

